[{"id":"VRCE-6-36-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":1,"english":"The rangers of woods, gazing at the earth and the sky, at length cast their eyes on the brothersRāma and Lakşmaņa covered all over with arrows. And after that Rākşasa had gone away having performed his work, like the God* going away, after having showered, there came to that place Vibhīşaņa with sugrīva. *Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0be17a083074bab58598756669f6199fc73a3ed5c33cfcb29faafed7026a386","compact":"c796ec1f4c726076d8217da6608aed84d8242a3dfd875427cbb0c544f2784a92","nasal":"c796ec1f4c726076d8217da6608aed84d8242a3dfd875427cbb0c544f2784a92"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":2,"english":"And mourning Raghu's sons, there also came in all haste Nila and Dvivida and Mainda and Sușeņa and Kumuda and Angada in company with Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"15c03233769aae0739079c745f0258b85eb41b50272958d58f3fbb0d03538de6","compact":"1cc82705475ecbcdde1bfc20d8f472244d7ab16aa143858fdb391f6986058c10","nasal":"1cc82705475ecbcdde1bfc20d8f472244d7ab16aa143858fdb391f6986058c10"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":3,"english":"And mourning Raghu's sons, there also came in all haste Nila and Dvivida and Mainda and Sușeņa and Kumuda and Angada in company with Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.426,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86228e962db356667ead0683e2ba4276724ecb2dafe7206d6a65c8c00da4d48a","compact":"d5f684eaaf1a9a3122bf1f84e20e4b4faba6655e4469143cd8f59507dc3cff49","nasal":"f357dea44d4075a40b81d51d0c4b376fcf474935a7146937f072e4ddc4a16b10"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":4,"english":"And moveless; breathing covered with bloodpierced all over with net-works of shafts; dumb; they* were lying on the field. *Rama and Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d682ec85fdc923f0e2b7e18102583299635ae58d41ab5c50d7205a4cacb7fd80","compact":"7647202ca568d8b1f7215b25ea2d3c8bf642abf4861deaa78c6c6ab9c8cdeb31","nasal":"96f34ceca4b07f9c176bb14975d69d8928b2b4b54cd895f2dff2862a5d7d6734"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":5,"english":"They were sighing like serpents; and were inert; and deprived of prowess; and washed in blood; and looking like to golden standards.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.574,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42c2bd2b49f7d4d24e5a3475c3aeffe877fbc5e4a63bc871b80fc157c53629b7","compact":"135b1bb3a924d332611c604cde2971a3940cc4db82630a936cfd98421c424e40","nasal":"19b2a795d84c2964a7e44ea7d3086b2d7e63f5ae61461feba3f3f41d23a4f5a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":6,"english":"And as they lay moveless, as become heroes, the leaders of monkeys environed them with tear-charged eyes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9cdd478d858346207150050a8bccd2c41e02e25e06092798d516a781bd9c22da","compact":"80253103d609de4e5fdda8d3ca2875afc91569069cb2790d10c25be3cbf7fa3a","nasal":"04f87ee62e6f9eb8bdef96edbec42c9108c25eb422d5affe245dccaf75ec4522"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":7,"english":"Seeing the sons of Raghu lying, covered with showers of shafts, the monkeys, with Vibhisana, were pained (exceedingly).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4f8f6945d270c9f9291ec951b84c7bbddd0900af685f31d6104d7deff9f8301","compact":"4fe257a9ad15ceb56170c2f128138ba6034c9a7d6ba7d227d7773fffcb27702d","nasal":"4fe257a9ad15ceb56170c2f128138ba6034c9a7d6ba7d227d7773fffcb27702d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":8,"english":"The monkeys, Surveying the sky as well as all directions, could not see Rāvana's son in battle enveloped with illusion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"762b4154d7052862b9d789af87426ed4cb01a74f7c5994723adfe2557ae06c47","compact":"13669964a1500f5a5bbd37287839a9c667467d53ffbe00897e83713fccd7c2f4","nasal":"8d16edae3035e2e1c84a0c5c8613639c5fc2a3e48b76813db85264f1641c6775"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":9,"english":"Then Vibhīşaņa by means of illusion saw his brother's son staying before, hidden by illusion. And Vibhīşaņa saw that hero of incomparable deeds, who had no compeer in the field and who had energy, fame and prowess-as he remained invisible in consequence of the boon received from Brahma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.625,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e95035562583668e0a894269e9ba0019cf61988cfb7d42d41c57ac46ce5462e2","compact":"44c931374351885baf297587bbef7184c4f3189c521189edd7742d19bb0e3255","nasal":"e9ee16540d6ddcfb07405de35db3dcfb6734c81efef337f5a50999cfc4d70616"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":10,"english":"Then Vibhīşaņa by means of illusion saw his brother's son staying before, hidden by illusion. And Vibhīşaņa saw that hero of incomparable deeds, who had no compeer in the field and who had energy, fame and prowess-as he remained invisible in consequence of the boon received from Brahma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2a5822ae5c9d59b9111981943f6c21db88f5309e41b7e4ce48ba938d28044b68","compact":"ed599505ea30f5c5d3fbbeb94d0d864b6770e9974a7c9aa70e526f3405f01b1c","nasal":"609bd88a291a12499c9b84cd0e5ab3fbe7c669b3d8134e4c5522a793c58672c0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":11,"english":"And Indrajit, seeing his own feat and them lying at length, spoke in excess of joy, gladdening all the Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6219a306bbf3e662f331f76b1d089718e05e66d922db3d20