a3992af71d14f252757d86e95e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":33,"english":"Or do you protect Rāma so long as he does not regain consciousness; and when the Kākutsthas shall have regained consciousness, all our apprehension shall vanish.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce6dde120ec4d7b6a839b0f72275e1b9d20063c6abcee5cd7f60e81a1b50be84","compact":"490098e9763990efa03cc1dddd099aac0dd44c7e8f55ac0c4945096d25cf6041","nasal":"490098e9763990efa03cc1dddd099aac0dd44c7e8f55ac0c4945096d25cf6041"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":34,"english":"This is nothing to Rāma is not dying. And Lakşmi* who is incapable of being attained by those that are doomed, shall not forsake this one. *The goddess of prosperity. to","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01e7caec9979484ac9d919dab3d3fb315f295d5d0ea2839e277bb6fc2c672996","compact":"a603d43ceb2b254c65316cba5a04697126c7092982d5f56142e463e17326ae93","nasal":"a603d43ceb2b254c65316cba5a04697126c7092982d5f56142e463e17326ae93"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-36-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":36,"verse":35,"english":"Therefore do you comfort yourself, do you also cheer up your own forces, while I am engaged in composing all the troops.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.725,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-46-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6036035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"82dfd868d227cec2e7c6ee099